WEBVTT

00:06:28.895 --> 00:06:32.653
and there's a quality of silence
that occurs none of the other times

00:06:32.677 --> 00:06:34.384
I go out and give speeches.

00:06:34.408 --> 00:06:37.670
And that's because people are really
emotionally and morally starved

00:06:37.694 --> 00:06:39.722
for someone who's willing to be vulnerable

00:06:39.746 --> 00:06:42.804
and someone who's willing to tell
about the real truths of life,

00:06:42.828 --> 00:06:44.851
which are not part of the common currency.

00:06:44.875 --> 00:06:47.698
We are overpoliticized in our culture
and undermoralized.

00:06:47.722 --> 00:06:50.949
We are not used to talking
about this stuff, especially guys.

00:06:50.973 --> 00:06:55.238
CA: A lot of people have noticed the shift
in you and your interests away from ...

00:06:55.262 --> 00:06:56.979
For many years, you were seen as

00:06:57.003 --> 00:07:01.073
the token right-of-center columnist
for "The New York Times,"